"Square root both sides (not a perfect square, so keep the √): x + 1 = ±√5":"Saca la raíz cuadrada de ambos lados (no es un cuadrado perfecto, así que deja el √): x + 1 = ±√5",
"Answer: x = −1 ± √5":"Respuesta: x = −1 ± √5",
"x² − 4x − 1 = 0  (leave a √ in it)":"x² − 4x − 1 = 0  (deja un √ en la respuesta)",
"Move the constant: x² − 4x = 1":"Pasa la constante: x² − 4x = 1",
"Half of −4 is −2, squared is 4 — add to both sides: (x − 2)² = 5":"La mitad de −4 es −2, y al cuadrado es 4; súmalo a ambos lados: (x − 2)² = 5",
"Square root both sides (not a perfect square, so keep the √): x − 2 = ±√5":"Saca la raíz cuadrada de ambos lados (no es un cuadrado perfecto, así que deja el √): x − 2 = ±√5",
"Answer: x = 2 ± √5":"Respuesta: x = 2 ± √5",
"The Quadratic Formula":"La fórmula cuadrática",
"The one method that solves ANY quadratic, even ones that don't factor nicely.":"El único método que resuelve CUALQUIER ecuación cuadrática, incluso las que no se factorizan fácilmente.",
"Write the equation as ax² + bx + c = 0 and identify a, b, and c (watch the signs!). Plug them into x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / (2a) and simplify carefully, one piece at a time.":"Escribe la ecuación como ax² + bx + c = 0 e identifica a, b y c (¡fíjate en los signos!). Sustitúyelos en x = (−b ± √(b² − 4ac)) / (2a) y simplifica con cuidado, una parte a la vez.",
"Discriminant":"Discriminante",
"The part under the square root in the quadratic formula, b² − 4ac.":"La parte que está debajo de la raíz cuadrada en la fórmula cuadrática, b² − 4ac.",
"For x² + 3x − 10 = 0, the discriminant is 9 + 40 = 49.":"Para x² + 3x − 10 = 0, el discriminante es 9 + 40 = 49.",
"Using the Formula":"Usar la fórmula",
"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>PURPLE</span> = a, b, c, <span class='ex-blue'>BLUE</span> = the discriminant, <span class='ex-red'>RED</span> = the answer</div>":"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>MORADO</span> = a, b, c, <span class='ex-blue'>AZUL</span> = el discriminante, <span class='ex-red'>ROJO</span> = la respuesta</div>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> Identify <span class='ex-purple'>a, b, c</span>: 2x² + 5x − 3 = 0 → a=2, b=5, c=−3":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> Identifica <span class='ex-purple'>a, b, c</span>: 2x² + 5x − 3 = 0 → a=2, b=5, c=−3",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Find the <span class='ex-blue'>discriminant</span>: b²−4ac = 25−(4)(2)(−3) = <span class='ex-blue'>49</span>, √49 = 7":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Halla el <span class='ex-blue'>discriminante</span>: b²−4ac = 25−(4)(2)(−3) = <span class='ex-blue'>49</span>, √49 = 7",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Plug into x = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>−b ± √(b²−4ac)</span><span class='frac-den'>2a</span></span> = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>−5 ± 7</span><span class='frac-den'>4</span></span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Sustituye en x = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>−b ± √(b²−4ac)</span><span class='frac-den'>2a</span></span> = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>−5 ± 7</span><span class='frac-den'>4</span></span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>x = 0.5 or x = −3</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>x = 0.5 o x = −3</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> Identify <span class='ex-purple'>a, b, c</span>: x² − x − 6 = 0 → a=1, b=−1, c=−6":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> Identifica <span class='ex-purple'>a, b, c</span>: x² − x − 6 = 0 → a=1, b=−1, c=−6",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Find the <span class='ex-blue'>discriminant</span>: 1−4(1)(−6) = <span class='ex-blue'>25</span>, √25 = 5":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Halla el <span class='ex-blue'>discriminante</span>: 1−4(1)(−6) = <span class='ex-blue'>25</span>, √25 = 5",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Plug in: x = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>1 ± 5</span><span class='frac-den'>2</span></span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Sustituye: x = <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>1 ± 5</span><span class='frac-den'>2</span></span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>x = 3 or x = −2</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>x = 3 o x = −2</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: the blue discriminant under the √ tells you the ± split — simplify it fully before you divide.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: el discriminante azul debajo del √ te dice cómo se separa el ±; simplifícalo por completo antes de dividir.</div>",
"When the Discriminant Isn't a Perfect Square":"Cuando el discriminante no es un cuadrado perfecto",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> Identify a, b, c: x² + 2x − 2 = 0 → a=1, b=2, c=−2":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> Identifica a, b, c: x² + 2x − 2 = 0 → a=1, b=2, c=−2",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Find the discriminant: b²−4ac = 4+8 = 12 — not a perfect square, so simplify the radical instead: √12 = 2√3":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Halla el discriminante: b²−4ac = 4+8 = 12; no es un cuadrado perfecto, así que simplifica el radical: √12 = 2√3",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Plug in: x = (−2 ± 2√3) / 2 = −1 ± √3":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Sustituye: x = (−2 ± 2√3) / 2 = −1 ± √3",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>x = −1 ± √3</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>x = −1 ± √3</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: when the discriminant isn't a perfect square, simplify its radical (like √12 = 2√3) and reduce the fraction — don't round it to a decimal.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: cuando el discriminante no es un cuadrado perfecto, simplifica su radical (como √12 = 2√3) y reduce la fracción; no lo redondees a un decimal.</div>",
