"Multi-Step Word Problems":"Problemas verbales de varios pasos",
"This is where algebra becomes useful — turning a real situation into an equation is the actual point.":"Aquí es donde el álgebra se vuelve útil: convertir una situación real en una ecuación es el verdadero objetivo.",
"Define a variable for the unknown. Translate the words into an equation piece by piece (\"% off\" means multiply by (1 − the rate); consecutive integers are x, x+1, x+2…). Solve the equation, then double-check you're answering the actual question being asked.":"Define una variable para lo desconocido. Traduce las palabras a una ecuación pieza por pieza (\"% de descuento\" significa multiplicar por (1 − la tasa); los enteros consecutivos son x, x+1, x+2…). Resuelve la ecuación y luego verifica que estés respondiendo la pregunta que realmente se hace.",
"Consecutive Integers":"Enteros consecutivos",
"Whole numbers that follow one after another.":"Números enteros que van uno detrás de otro.",
"5, 6, 7 are consecutive integers.":"5, 6, 7 son enteros consecutivos.",
"Simple Interest":"Interés simple",
"Interest calculated only on the original amount, using I = Prt (Principal × rate × time).":"Interés calculado solo sobre la cantidad original, usando I = Prt (capital × tasa × tiempo).",
"$500 at 4% for 3 years earns $60.":"$500 al 4% durante 3 años ganan $60.",
"Percent Off":"Porcentaje de descuento",
"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>PURPLE</span> = the percent you actually pay, <span class='ex-blue'>BLUE</span> = the original price, <span class='ex-red'>RED</span> = the answer</div>":"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>MORADO</span> = el porcentaje que realmente pagas, <span class='ex-blue'>AZUL</span> = el precio original, <span class='ex-red'>ROJO</span> = la respuesta</div>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> A $50 jacket is marked down 20% → you pay <span class='ex-purple'>80%</span> of the price":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> Una chaqueta de $50 tiene 20% de descuento → pagas el <span class='ex-purple'>80%</span> del precio",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Sale price = <span class='ex-blue'>50</span> × 0.80":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Precio de oferta = <span class='ex-blue'>50</span> × 0.80",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>$40</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>$40</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: \"X% off\" means you PAY (100 − X)%, not X% — a common slip.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: \"X% de descuento\" significa que PAGAS (100 − X)%, no X%; es un error muy común.</div>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> Let <span class='ex-purple'>x, x+1</span> be the two consecutive integers":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> Sean <span class='ex-purple'>x, x+1</span> los dos enteros consecutivos",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Translate \"sum is 25\" into an equation: <span class='ex-blue'>x + (x+1) = 25</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Traduce \"la suma es 25\" a una ecuación: <span class='ex-blue'>x + (x+1) = 25</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Solve: 2x + 1 = 25 → 2x = 24 → x = 12":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Resuelve: 2x + 1 = 25 → 2x = 24 → x = 12",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>the integers are 12 and 13</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>los enteros son 12 y 13</span>",
