"Answer: 3x² + 10x − 8":"Respuesta: 3x² + 10x − 8",
"Factoring Trinomials (a = 1)":"Factorizar trinomios (a = 1)",
"The most common factoring pattern you'll see — it's the reverse of FOIL, and it's the setup for solving quadratics by factoring.":"El patrón de factorización más común que verás — es lo inverso de FOIL y es la base para resolver cuadráticas por factorización.",
"For x² + bx + c, find two numbers that MULTIPLY to c and ADD to b. Write the factored form as (x + first number)(x + second number), keeping each number's own sign.":"Para x² + bx + c, busca dos números que MULTIPLIQUEN a c y SUMEN b. Escribe la forma factorizada como (x + primer número)(x + segundo número), conservando el signo de cada número.",
"x² + 5x + 6 is a trinomial.":"x² + 5x + 6 es un trinomio.",
"Both Factors Positive":"Ambos factores positivos",
"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>PURPLE</span> = the two numbers you're hunting for, <span class='ex-blue'>BLUE</span> = the check (multiply & add), <span class='ex-red'>RED</span> = the answer</div>":"<div class='ex-legend'><span class='ex-purple'>MORADO</span> = los dos números que buscas, <span class='ex-blue'>AZUL</span> = la comprobación (multiplicar y sumar), <span class='ex-red'>ROJO</span> = la respuesta</div>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> x² + 7x + 12 — need two numbers that multiply to 12 and add to 7: <span class='ex-purple'>3 and 4</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> x² + 7x + 12 — necesitas dos números que multipliquen a 12 y sumen 7: <span class='ex-purple'>3 y 4</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Check: <span class='ex-blue'>3 × 4 = 12 ✓, 3 + 4 = 7 ✓</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Comprueba: <span class='ex-blue'>3 × 4 = 12 ✓, 3 + 4 = 7 ✓</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>(x + 3)(x + 4)</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>(x + 3)(x + 4)</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: both numbers are positive because both c and b are positive.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: ambos números son positivos porque tanto c como b son positivos.</div>",
"A Negative Factor":"Un factor negativo",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> x² + 2x − 15 — need two numbers that multiply to −15 and add to 2: <span class='ex-purple'>5 and −3</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> x² + 2x − 15 — necesitas dos números que multipliquen a −15 y sumen 2: <span class='ex-purple'>5 y −3</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Check: <span class='ex-blue'>5 × (−3) = −15 ✓, 5 + (−3) = 2 ✓</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Comprueba: <span class='ex-blue'>5 × (−3) = −15 ✓, 5 + (−3) = 2 ✓</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>(x + 5)(x − 3)</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>(x + 5)(x − 3)</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: a NEGATIVE c means the two numbers have opposite signs; a positive c means they match.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: una c NEGATIVA significa que los dos números tienen signos opuestos; una c positiva significa que tienen el mismo signo.</div>",
