"Rational Expression Operations":"Operaciones con expresiones racionales",
"The same multiply/divide/add/subtract rules you use with number fractions — but you have to factor first to find what actually cancels.":"Las mismas reglas de multiplicar, dividir, sumar y restar que usas con fracciones numéricas — pero tienes que factorizar primero para ver qué se cancela de verdad.",
"Multiply: factor everything, then cancel any factor shared top-and-bottom across BOTH fractions. Divide: flip the second fraction (multiply by its reciprocal), then proceed like multiplication. Add/Subtract: get a common denominator first, then combine the numerators only. Just like simplifying a single rational expression, finish by stating the restriction: any x-value that would make an ORIGINAL denominator — or, when dividing, the fraction you flipped — equal 0 stays off-limits.":"Multiplicar: factoriza todo y luego cancela cualquier factor compartido entre el numerador y el denominador de AMBAS fracciones. Dividir: voltea la segunda fracción (multiplica por su recíproco) y luego procede como en la multiplicación. Sumar/restar: primero consigue un denominador común y luego combina solo los numeradores. Igual que al simplificar una sola expresión racional, termina indicando la restricción: cualquier valor de x que haga que un denominador ORIGINAL — o, al dividir, la fracción que volteaste — sea igual a 0 queda prohibido.",
"Reciprocal":"Recíproco",
"A fraction flipped upside down.":"Una fracción puesta al revés.",
"The reciprocal of (x+1)/x is x/(x+1).":"El recíproco de (x+1)/x es x/(x+1).",
"Common Denominator":"Denominador común",
"A denominator shared by two fractions, needed before adding or subtracting them.":"Un denominador compartido por dos fracciones, necesario antes de sumarlas o restarlas.",
"To add 1/x and 1/3, the common denominator is 3x.":"Para sumar 1/x y 1/3, el denominador común es 3x.",
"Multiplying Rational Expressions":"Multiplicar expresiones racionales",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x</span><span class='frac-den'>x+2</span></span> × <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+2</span><span class='frac-den'>3</span></span> — multiply straight across: <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x(x+2)</span><span class='frac-den'>3(x+2)</span></span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x</span><span class='frac-den'>x+2</span></span> × <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+2</span><span class='frac-den'>3</span></span> — multiplica directo: <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x(x+2)</span><span class='frac-den'>3(x+2)</span></span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Cancel the shared factor <span class='ex-purple'>(x+2)</span> top and bottom":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Cancela el factor compartido <span class='ex-purple'>(x+2)</span> arriba y abajo",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Restriction: <span class='ex-blue'>x+2</span> = 0 when x = −2":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Restricción: <span class='ex-blue'>x+2</span> = 0 cuando x = −2",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-red'>x/3, where x ≠ −2</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-red'>x/3, donde x ≠ −2</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: multiply across first, THEN look for anything to cancel — but the restriction still comes from the ORIGINAL denominator.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: primero multiplica directo, LUEGO busca qué cancelar — pero la restricción sigue saliendo del denominador ORIGINAL.</div>",
"Dividing Rational Expressions":"Dividir expresiones racionales",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 1:</span> <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+1</span><span class='frac-den'>2</span></span> ÷ <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+1</span><span class='frac-den'>4</span></span> — flip the second fraction and multiply: <span class='ex-purple'>× 4/(x+1)</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 1:</span> <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+1</span><span class='frac-den'>2</span></span> ÷ <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>x+1</span><span class='frac-den'>4</span></span> — voltea la segunda fracción y multiplica: <span class='ex-purple'>× 4/(x+1)</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 2:</span> Multiply across: <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>(x+1)·4</span><span class='frac-den'>2·(x+1)</span></span>, then cancel <span class='ex-purple'>(x+1)</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 2:</span> Multiplica directo: <span class='frac'><span class='frac-num'>(x+1)·4</span><span class='frac-den'>2·(x+1)</span></span>, luego cancela <span class='ex-purple'>(x+1)</span>",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 3:</span> Restriction: <span class='ex-blue'>x+1</span> = 0 when x = −1":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 3:</span> Restricción: <span class='ex-blue'>x+1</span> = 0 cuando x = −1",
"<span class='step-label'>Step 4:</span> Answer: <span class='ex-blue'>4/2 simplifies to</span> <span class='ex-red'>2, where x ≠ −1</span>":"<span class='step-label'>Paso 4:</span> Respuesta: <span class='ex-blue'>4/2 se simplifica a</span> <span class='ex-red'>2, donde x ≠ −1</span>",
"<div class='ex-notice'>Notice: dividing fractions always starts with \"flip the second one and multiply\" — and the fraction you flipped is where the restriction comes from.</div>":"<div class='ex-notice'>Fíjate: dividir fracciones siempre empieza con \"voltea la segunda y multiplica\" — y la fracción que volteaste es de donde sale la restricción.</div>",
